Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.45,0:00:03.93,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.93,0:00:07.14,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,The restoration of your right \Nto succeed the throne?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.48,0:00:11.79,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yes. I've been removed from my duties \Nas princess for a long time,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.79,0:00:16.11,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,so I thought I should reintroduce \Nmyself to the spirit-faithful.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.11,0:00:19.25,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,I see! That is quite admirable.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.25,0:00:23.70,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,It seems our tomboy princess \Nhas settled down at last.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.70,0:00:27.92,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,Do you intend to assume the role \Nof our future queen from now on?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.60,0:00:30.39,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yes... I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.83,0:00:32.21,Default,LeaderA,0,0,0,,Is she mad?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.21,0:00:36.13,Default,LeaderA,0,0,0,,We've never had a queen, much less \Na royal who couldn't use magic!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.13,0:00:39.09,Default,LeaderB,0,0,0,,The king isn't even forty years old yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.09,0:00:41.47,Default,LeaderB,0,0,0,,He could still produce \Na new heir if he tried.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.47,0:00:47.20,Default,LeaderA,0,0,0,,Yes, a king has an obligation to produce \Nand raise his heir, for crying out loud!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.68,0:00:53.67,Default,Middle Elder,0,0,0,,He must have some profound idea in mind \Nthat we lower classes could never fathom.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.67,0:00:54.90,Default,Middle Elder,0,0,0,,Either that,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.90,0:00:58.85,Default,Middle Elder,0,0,0,,or he just really wants \NPrincess Anisphia to be queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.73,0:01:03.00,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Regardless of what the king may be thinking,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.00,0:01:07.32,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I intend to carry out my duties \Nrespectably as the next in line.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.69,0:01:10.83,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I would greatly appreciate your cooperation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.72,0:01:17.10,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,You have made your determination \Nquite clear to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.10,0:01:19.89,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,We look forward to seeing how \Nyou conduct yourself henceforth.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.64,0:01:25.35,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yes. I humbly request your \Nguidance and encouragement.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.35,0:01:26.82,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.43,0:01:30.48,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,However, may I say just one thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.66,0:01:34.15,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,Your... "magicology," was it?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.15,0:01:35.91,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,It is unacceptable.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.18,0:01:42.60,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,To give magic, a blessing granted \Nonly to us, to mere commoners
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.60,0:01:47.38,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,would render the authority of \Nthe nobility and royalty useless.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.82,0:01:49.82,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,Do you understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.55,0:01:53.46,Default,Middle Elder,0,0,0,,No need for concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.46,0:01:57.14,Default,Middle Elder,0,0,0,,The princess has always \Nloved magic, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.90,0:02:04.47,Default,LeaderA,0,0,0,,Which means she will need to think of a way \Nto give magic to the next generation.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.47,0:02:07.96,Default,LeaderB,0,0,0,,Exactly. The royal family \Nexists for the purpose
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.96,0:02:10.32,Default,LeaderB,0,0,0,,of inheriting the gift of \Nmagic from the spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.56,0:02:15.53,Default,Middle Elder,0,0,0,,Meaning it would be ideal for the princess \Nto produce an heir as soon as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.99,0:02:20.00,Default,LeaderB,0,0,0,,In that case, we shall \Nhave to choose a partner
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.00,0:02:22.70,Default,LeaderB,0,0,0,,close to her age from a high-ranking family.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.06,0:02:25.96,Default,LeaderA,0,0,0,,At this point, why prioritize status?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.96,0:02:29.21,Default,LeaderA,0,0,0,,We can just choose someone with \Nan exceptional talent for magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.21,0:02:32.41,Default,LeaderB,0,0,0,,Then there's no need to worry \Nabout his age, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.68,0:02:36.73,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,Indeed. We should keep a \Nfew candidates on hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.73,0:02:41.68,Default,High Elder,0,0,0,,Luckily, the princess seems \Nto be in magnificent health.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.84,0:02:48.98,Default,Middle Elder,0,0,0,,That said, I suppose internal stability \Nshould be our first priority.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.98,0:02:49.77,Default,LeaderA,0,0,0,,True.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.77,0:02:52.21,Default,LeaderB,0,0,0,,Yes, but we must waste no time...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.41,0:03:08.68,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.66,0:03:11.39,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm perfectly fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.46,0:04:42.01,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2}The Magical Revolution
Dialogue: 1,0:04:33.46,0:04:42.01,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2\clip(m 116 13 l 113 58 331 59 328 30 310 58 116 56 120 14 238 18 218 44 192 6 357 14 332 43 331 5 535 5 525 55 473 55 492 25)}The {\c&H7A4AE4&}Mag{\c&HE38B59&}ical {\c&H7A4AE4&}Revol{\c&HE38B59&}ution
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.46,0:04:42.01,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\fs15\pos(320,56)\blur2}of the {\c&H7A4AE4&}Reincarnated Princess {\c&H140900&}and the {\c&HE38B59&}Genius Young Lady
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.43,0:04:46.22,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Here you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.69,0:04:47.93,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.69,0:04:52.84,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,You've truly begun \Nto look the part of a maid.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.13,0:04:55.46,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,I'm still in training...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.46,0:04:57.06,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,But I have you to thank, Miss Ilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.06,0:05:00.73,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,You have been an apprentice \Nworth teaching, Lainie.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.29,0:05:10.65,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis, may I have some time \Nto speak with you tomorrow?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.71,0:05:14.67,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Ilia and Lainie, I'd like you there, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.17,0:05:23.13,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Um, I have Tilty's medical exam tomorrow...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.69,0:05:29.61,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'll reschedule it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.61,0:05:31.22,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.01,0:05:35.43,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I've found what it is that I must do.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.43,0:05:40.80,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,And I want you, along with your father \Nand mother, to hear it first.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.19,0:05:55.99,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Ah, there you are, Anis.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.44,0:06:02.39,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Father, who is she?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.98,0:06:05.43,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Pleased to meet you, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.43,0:06:06.92,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,I'm Lumi.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.92,0:06:09.34,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,If I called myself a spirit contractor, \Nwould you understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.34,0:06:13.67,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh?! But... what is a spirit \Ncontractor doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.51,0:06:20.36,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Your Majesties, thank you for making time \Nto meet with me today.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.71,0:06:22.56,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,It's no bother at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.98,0:06:26.63,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,But I do wonder what it \Nis you want to tell us...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.55,0:06:35.85,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I have a favor I wish to ask of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.85,0:06:36.95,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Uh-huh...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.69,0:06:41.93,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Lumi has determined that I meet the \Nrequirements to forge a spirit contract.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.36,0:06:43.87,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.66,0:06:51.76,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh? A s-spirit contract? Euphie?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.76,0:06:53.04,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.04,0:06:57.72,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,She is the only one in the world right now \Nwith the qualifications and will to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.40,0:06:59.68,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Are you serious?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.77,0:07:05.51,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Even knowing the truth of what \Nspirit contractors are?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.51,0:07:06.32,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.74,0:07:13.54,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Becoming a spirit contractor will make it \Ndifficult for you to live a normal life.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.99,0:07:16.37,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What do you mean by that?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.43,0:07:20.51,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,How old does Miss Lumi look to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.20,0:07:26.37,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,How old? About the same as me?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.96,0:07:31.84,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,She still looks exactly the way \Nshe did when we first met her.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.27,0:07:33.84,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,That was decades ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.11,0:07:38.80,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,So spirit contractors... never age?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.06,0:07:43.01,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Well, yes, but it's more than just that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.27,0:07:47.06,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,In exchange for receiving great power, \Nthe contract dictates
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.06,0:07:49.74,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,that you will eventually \Nbecome a spirit yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.74,0:07:51.98,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You'll... become a spirit?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.27,0:07:57.85,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,My real name is Lumielle René Palettia.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.85,0:08:00.41,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,In other words, I'm your ancestor.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.41,0:08:03.12,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Ancestor? You mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.49,0:08:10.79,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,I had a prince consort, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.47,0:08:14.57,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,He was a good man. A very good man.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.62,0:08:21.71,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,There were times when I wished \NI could live with him forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.76,0:08:24.94,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.21,0:08:29.99,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,The difference between our lifespans \Nkilled any hope of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.80,0:08:32.37,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Once you become a spirit,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.37,0:08:35.85,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,all desires you had as a human disappear.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.68,0:08:40.35,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,There's no more need \Nfor memories or emotions.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.13,0:08:45.83,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Can you imagine that? You forget {\i1}everything{\i0}.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.49,0:08:48.79,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,The way they smile at you in exasperation,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.57,0:08:51.76,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,the sound of their voice \Nsoftly calling your name,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.72,0:08:55.24,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,the warmth you feel when \Nthey shyly touch you...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.55,0:08:58.63,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,You forget all of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.68,0:09:07.46,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,However you may try \Nto preserve it all in writing,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.46,0:09:09.51,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,it only survives on paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.41,0:09:15.06,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,It becomes no more than a record \Nwith no feelings attached to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.32,0:09:21.03,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,You even forget that you forgot it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.49,0:09:25.44,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,You lose your human body, your human life,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.87,0:09:28.94,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,and in time, even your human soul...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.92,0:09:32.59,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,and find yourself trapped \Nin eternal solitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.05,0:09:43.05,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That's... the truth of the spirit contract?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.99,0:09:47.10,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Knowing that, do you still wish to forge one?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.55,0:09:53.58,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Yes. The spirit contract \Nis essential in fulfilling my wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.90,0:09:58.82,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, once I have \Ncompleted the spirit contract,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.82,0:10:02.11,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I would like you to adopt me \Ninto the royal family
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.11,0:10:04.79,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,and grant me the right \Nto inherit the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.56,0:10:06.24,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.55,0:10:12.37,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,W-Wait, wait! What are you saying?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.37,0:10:15.29,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Adopt you?! Why would you ask that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.06,0:10:21.38,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Grantz! What's the meaning of this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.38,0:10:23.85,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Why would Euphyllia ask such a thing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.85,0:10:26.07,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I never gave her my blessing to ask this.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.07,0:10:29.97,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,But you know she isn't the type \Nto take no for an answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.32,0:10:31.81,DefaultTop,Grantz,0,0,0,,She {\i1}is{\i0} my daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.73,0:10:33.63,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie... Why would you...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.55,0:10:38.41,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Because I cannot allow you to become queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.92,0:10:42.53,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Wh-Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.53,0:10:44.67,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What do you mean by that, Euphyllia?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.07,0:10:49.02,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis will never be accepted \Nby the nobility of this kingdom,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.02,0:10:52.56,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,for the sole reason that \Nshe cannot use magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.13,0:10:56.63,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,And that's why you want me to \Ngive you the right to succeed?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.46,0:11:02.80,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I acknowledge that you \Nhave remarkable talent.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.80,0:11:06.47,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,But even if we adopt you, that doesn't \Nguarantee the nobles will accept you!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.78,0:11:09.42,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,That's what the spirit contract is for.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.42,0:11:12.58,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,If I achieve the same thing \Nour founding king did,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.58,0:11:16.06,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I can convince the spirit-faithful \Nto accept me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.03,0:11:20.22,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie, why?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.74,0:11:23.95,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,So that you won't have to be queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.22,0:11:27.92,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Wait... Hang on! \NI never asked you to do this!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.15,0:11:32.56,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I know. This is a promise \Nthat I made my own decision to fulfill.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.97,0:11:35.12,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I don't want you to become queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.03,0:11:37.34,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Are you serious about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.37,0:11:44.36,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But you won't be human anymore!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.36,0:11:46.86,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You'll lose everyone, forget everything,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.86,0:11:49.01,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,and be alone for the rest of eternity!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.43,0:11:53.25,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You can't do that!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.86,0:11:56.85,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'd rather be queen than let you...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.20,0:12:04.08,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Do you truly believe that you can \Nlead this kingdom as its queen?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.18,0:12:14.53,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You're right. I don't have \Nthe ability to use magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.04,0:12:18.50,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And I know the nobles of this \Nkingdom will never accept me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.92,0:12:22.90,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But that's no reason for you \Nto take this upon yourself!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.90,0:12:25.38,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Still, if I become queen,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.38,0:12:27.98,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'll be able to keep your dream alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.30,0:12:31.48,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Don't you love magic and want to share it
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.48,0:12:35.26,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,so that more people can understand \Nhow wonderful it is?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.59,0:12:37.69,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Wasn't that your dream?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.40,0:12:40.66,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,My dream...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.01,0:12:43.85,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I want you to achieve your dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.85,0:12:47.61,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Your dream will bring \Nprosperity to this kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.14,0:12:51.01,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Please allow me to share \Nyour dream with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.01,0:12:55.58,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,For you to be free is my hope and wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.59,0:13:01.64,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,So, Miss Anis, please take my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.77,0:13:13.01,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.26,0:13:16.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Don't talk like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.80,0:13:18.60,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Don't make me depend on you!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.57,0:13:20.65,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.07,0:13:23.18,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm the princess!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.18,0:13:26.87,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Whether they accept me or not, \NI'm this kingdom's princess!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.23,0:13:31.89,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If you take even that away from me...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.31,0:13:35.83,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What value will I have left?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.92,0:13:38.48,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Anis...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.15,0:13:48.78,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Wait, Anis!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.78,0:13:50.09,Default,Sylphine,0,0,0,,Anisphia!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.44,0:14:08.53,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,What in the world are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.89,0:14:14.33,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Tilty... Why...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.55,0:14:17.60,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You're the one who told me \Nto make a house call.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.60,0:14:21.21,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Do you have any idea what a spectacle \Nyou're making of yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.21,0:14:23.58,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I could tell it was you \Nfrom inside my carriage.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.17,0:14:26.16,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Ugh, you're such a pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.02,0:14:31.11,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Can you stand?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.56,0:14:32.41,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.41,0:14:35.71,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,What did I tell you? \NYou're making a scene. Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.82,0:14:37.64,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Right...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.40,0:14:55.43,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Go home once you've calmed down.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.43,0:14:57.66,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Or should I call someone to come get you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.38,0:15:00.54,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Sorry. Don't do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.54,0:15:01.74,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Not yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.35,0:15:04.01,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,What a pain...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.41,0:15:09.21,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Aren't you supposed to just silently \Ncomfort me at times like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.57,0:15:12.03,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,What do you expect out of me?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.03,0:15:15.06,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Go home before this blows up into \Na big mess. You're a nuisance.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.93,0:15:17.02,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,A nuisance...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.36,0:15:20.98,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.43,0:15:23.72,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You're really throwing me off here...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.60,0:15:29.46,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Stay as long as you want.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.45,0:15:31.30,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.71,0:15:34.25,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,But when someone comes for you, go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.03,0:15:36.16,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Will anyone come?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.77,0:15:40.29,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,If they don't, you could \Njust stay here, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.61,0:15:44.95,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I'll hear you out, at least \Nwhenever I have the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.50,0:15:53.51,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.02,0:15:57.76,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I thought you didn't care about \Nyour right to the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.52,0:16:00.21,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I didn't care.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.71,0:16:02.99,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But Al isn't around anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.99,0:16:07.48,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm the one who has to take on \Nthe responsibility of ruling.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.43,0:16:11.37,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If I don't, I have no value as a princess.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.81,0:16:16.51,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,So how could she tell me I don't \Nhave to be queen after all this?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.47,0:16:19.62,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But I have to give in.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.14,0:16:21.92,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,They'll never accept me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.45,0:16:26.50,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Why do you need them to accept you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.84,0:16:27.57,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.23,0:16:31.80,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,A stupid father who dumps all the \Nresponsibility on his daughter...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.80,0:16:35.96,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,A bunch of stupid nobles who give thanks \Nfor some moldy old traditions...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.96,0:16:38.77,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,A stupid kingdom that \Ndoesn't appreciate you...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.77,0:16:41.43,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Why do you need any of them to accept you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.26,0:16:45.01,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But... But still...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.90,0:16:45.64,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Oh, come on...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.81,0:16:56.54,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Why don't you just ditch this kingdom?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.97,0:16:59.08,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Throw away your role \Nand your right to the throne,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.08,0:17:02.87,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,and go somewhere completely \Ndifferent to study magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.27,0:17:05.74,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You don't need to be here to do that, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.27,0:17:08.22,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.49,0:17:12.40,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,If you'd be missing any documents \Nor materials, I can help you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.86,0:17:15.88,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,It might be nice to travel \Nto all kinds of places together.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.29,0:17:19.33,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,We could study the magic and curses \Nthey have in other countries,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.78,0:17:21.82,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,eat some delicious foods here and there,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.21,0:17:27.19,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,and maybe con some money out of \Nevil nobles and corrupt merchants.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.00,0:17:29.81,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That sounds nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.06,0:17:33.25,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But we can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.53,0:17:36.57,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I still can't throw it away.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.57,0:17:38.82,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I can't throw away the fact \Nthat I'm a princess.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.25,0:17:41.18,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.97,0:17:45.29,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Tilty! Are you in there?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.29,0:17:46.72,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,If you are, please answer me!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.20,0:17:49.13,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Someone came for you after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.22,0:17:55.13,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.45,0:18:06.22,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.00,0:18:13.07,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I'll leave the room. Tell me before you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.07,0:18:16.26,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm very sorry for all the trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.56,0:18:25.87,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Just leave me alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.40,0:18:28.53,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I can't do that!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.28,0:18:39.12,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Why are you making that face?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.98,0:18:43.91,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,That's the first time you've \Nexpressed anger toward me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.31,0:18:45.00,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.94,0:18:54.67,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Being a princess was much more important \Nto you than I realized, wasn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.38,0:19:05.18,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You're not fair, Euphie!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.72,0:19:08.32,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I wanted the ability to use magic, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.26,0:19:13.98,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Then I wouldn't have to lose \Nanyone... or anything...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.26,0:19:19.00,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Why do you have to deprive me \Nof my role as princess {\i1}now{\i0}?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.59,0:19:23.46,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's my duty... and it's all I have left!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.02,0:19:27.38,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Even if no one approves \Nor expects anything of me,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.38,0:19:29.43,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm the princess of this kingdom!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.76,0:19:32.39,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm the daughter of my mother and father!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.46,0:19:35.62,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I can still keep trying hard...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.36,0:19:38.27,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I can try harder!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.27,0:19:41.81,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,So don't make me someone nobody needs!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.51,0:19:53.95,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's okay. I'm perfectly fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.30,0:19:57.56,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You're obviously not fine at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.59,0:20:01.35,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Someone who values others before herself,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.35,0:20:03.31,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,who can't leave them on their own,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.31,0:20:06.20,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,who'd even sacrifice herself for them...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.19,0:20:10.78,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,To be rejected and hated by everyone...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.69,0:20:14.47,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,There's no way you're fine with that!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.84,0:20:16.11,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.80,0:20:19.01,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,None of this is your fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.41,0:20:24.15,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,This kingdom where you can't make anyone \Nhappy without magic is to blame!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.15,0:20:29.14,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But even so, this is the kingdom that my \Nmother and father wanted to protect!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.54,0:20:34.05,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And all I can do is ruin that...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.88,0:20:39.13,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But you have protected it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.52,0:20:42.79,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,With the power of magic that \Nyou had more faith in than anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.28,0:20:46.00,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You care about this kingdom \Nmore than anyone,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.00,0:20:49.03,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,and you've fought for it \Nby yourself all this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.51,0:20:51.83,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Even without anyone's approval,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.83,0:20:56.41,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,you made your very own \Nkind of magic a reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.62,0:21:02.20,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You have my affirmation \Nabove all others, Miss Anis.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.77,0:21:16.58,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's okay now. You've done enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.85,0:21:20.24,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I can give up now.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.89,0:21:24.38,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie, the one I admire most \Nof all, gave me her approval.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.96,0:21:27.00,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That's more than rewarding enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.60,0:21:29.05,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.47,0:21:33.31,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I still can't do it. \NI don't want to sacrifice you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.77,0:21:37.73,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,My dream can't even begin \Nto compare to your life.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.00,0:21:39.44,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But—
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.83,0:21:43.59,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I know you won't back down,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.59,0:21:46.15,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I know how you feel, \Nand I know what you're saying.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.85,0:21:50.83,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,So... let's have a duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.89,0:21:56.00,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That's how you can convince me.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.25,0:22:02.49,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Very well.
